# Line endings.
#
# Git normalises to LF in the repository and converts on checkout according to
# whatever core.autocrlf happens to be set to on a given machine. For two files
# that is not a preference, it is a correctness requirement:
#
#   *.cmd  cmd.exe misparses an LF-only batch file in a way that STILL RUNS --
#          it split a "-m" out of a later line into a phantom command and
#          printed "'m' is not recognized" before carrying on. A launcher that
#          half-works is worse than one that does not.
#
#   *.ps1  PowerShell tolerates LF, but a here-string terminator is matched at
#          the start of a line and the failure modes are similarly quiet.
#
# Everything else follows the platform default.

*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
